  "prompt": "For each month from February to December 2024, give LedgerLoop's logo churn rate as a percentage: 100 times the accounts that churned in the month divided by the accounts with MRR at the end of the month before, rounded to 2 decimals with ROUND (1.45 for 1.45%). The base of a month is the accounts with MRR at the end of the month before: those with a row in mrr_monthly for the month before (mrr_monthly.month is the first day of a month). An account churned in a month when it has a churn event (event_type churn in subscription_events) dated in that month; count each account once. An account that starts or comes back during the month is not in that month's base. Return two columns, in this order: month_start (the first day of the month) and churn_pct. Return one row for each of the 11 months; a month with no churn shows 0. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
